{"id":"9ljalyrf","ord":"a0","title":"roadmap.olai"}
{"id":"wtanceuk","parent":"9ljalyrf","ord":"a0","title":"Viewing"}
{"id":"wikilinks","parent":"wtanceuk","ord":"a0","title":"[[Wikilinks]] in documents resolve to links — today they render as literal text","desc":"Filed 2026-08-12 on the human's word (separate item, not folded into daily-notes).\n\n- **Problem:** their vault's notes lean on Obsidian-style [[target]] and [[target|label]], which olai's markdown pipeline currently renders as literal bracket text (visible in the human's daily-note screenshot).\n- **Scope:** resolve wikilinks at render time in the sanitising pipeline (markdown/render.ts + rewrite.ts territory).\n  - [[target|label]] shows label, [[target]] shows target.\n  - **Resolution order:** a served document whose basename or path matches → /doc/<path>; a node id match → /n/<id>.\n  - Unresolved stays visibly distinct (muted, title says unresolved — never silently a dead link, per HACKING error-surfacing).\n  - Inline-only contexts (node titles via title.ts) get the same treatment.\n- **Tests:** over the resolution table and the sanitiser (a wikilink must not open an injection seam).\n- Depends on nothing in flight; touches markdown/ only.\n- NOT DISPATCHED.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"5kz73j46","parent":"9ljalyrf","ord":"a1","title":"Agents"}
{"id":"47ps3bzc","parent":"5kz73j46","ord":"a0","title":"Orchestrate from the chat, not a terminal #human"}
{"id":"oic-wake","parent":"47ps3bzc","ord":"a0","title":"Nothing can wake a chat agent — the babysitting regression","todo":true,"desc":"Nothing can wake a chat agent — the babysitting regression.\n\n- ACP turns are human-initiated.\n- No MCP notification wakes an idle session.\n- The MCP blocking waits (wait_agentState / wait_outputSettled) hold a turn open into the host's timeout.\n- **Answered in design 2026-08-15** (the human asked \"can kolu MCP do this?\" — yes, with the right subscriber): the subscriber does not have to be the agent.\n  - Olai's server is the ACP CLIENT — the party that starts turns.\n  - kolu MCP exposes subscribable snapshot-bearing resources: `urgency` (who needs attention) and `terminals` (per-terminal agent state), per kolu-mcp/src/expose.ts.\n  - **Wake path:** kolu → olai's own subscription → olai starts a chat turn saying which lane settled.\n  - That build is the olai-subscribes node; this node closes when it lands.\n  - **Known sharp edge** for the first probe: kolu's `activity` resource cannot honor the read contract (fresh-subscriber-starts-empty, recorded in expose.ts:80) — urgency/terminals are the cells to lean on.\n- Until then, babysitting stays the terminal orchestrator's detached watchers.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"oic-shell","parent":"47ps3bzc","ord":"a1","title":"\"No shell, so no gh\" — contradicted; one live probe decides","todo":true,"desc":"FILED as \"No shell, so no gh\" — and CONTRADICTED 2026-08-15 by the human and by the code.\n\n- **Why wrong:** the claim counted only the MCP servers the session is handed (olai's ops, kolu's) and forgot the agent's own built-ins.\n- The chat runs the Claude Code adapter in bypassPermissions mode (interpret.ts:43, the 2026-08-09 design).\n- Nothing puts Bash in disallowedTools (only AskUserQuestion gets that, and olai avoids it via elicitation.form) — so the built-in shell, and gh with it, should run without asking.\n- **Probe:** one live probe settles it — in a real chat session, run `gh pr checks` and confirm the tool call executes rather than stalls on a permission nobody can answer.\n  - If it runs, this node closes as wrong and the chat orchestrator's gh story is already whole.\n  - The original desc's real observations that survive either way — fs_readFile being repo-scoped, TUI screens truncating long reviews — matter only if the probe fails.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"c8ruks63","parent":"47ps3bzc","ord":"a2","title":"Org-style properties: facts stop living in desc strings #needs-brainstorm"}
{"id":"props-parity","parent":"c8ruks63","ord":"a0","title":"PR: set_prop + prop: search + the drawer — both faces in one change","todo":true,"desc":"The user-facing half, full parity in one PR per the ruling.\n\n- **set_prop:** null removes; refuses every system key toward its own verb.\n  - status → the mark verbs\n  - date → set_date\n  - after → set_after\n  - created/changed → nothing, they are stamps\n- **Search:** learns prop:key and prop:key=value.\n- **Web:** gets the quiet drawer under the note (hidden when empty) with ••• menu add/edit/remove.\n- **Prototype to build against:** https://claude.ai/code/artifact/48a09a59-5079-44fe-b99a-7f3a5fe49c90 (insertion order, not alphabetical).\n- **Open question** to settle in this PR's design: whether search HITS carry props (one query = the lane board).","after":["props-floor"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"props-stamps","parent":"c8ruks63","ord":"a1","title":"PR: created + changed — the ops layer stamps, nothing else may","todo":true,"desc":"Workflowy's pair as the third kind of built-in.\n\n- Capture stamps `created`; every write op re-stamps `changed`.\n- No verb exists for either, and set_prop refuses both.\n- Absent on migrated nodes — the ledger does not invent a past; git log is the archaeologist's tool.\n- Display rides the drawer (props-parity), so this PR is ops-layer stamping plus the two rows appearing.","after":["props-floor"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"sbcbh1v3","parent":"9ljalyrf","ord":"a2","title":"Bugs"}
{"id":"socket-litter","parent":"sbcbh1v3","ord":"a0","title":"Servers never unlink their unix socket — 7,305 dead ones found","doing":true,"desc":"Found 2026-08-15 root-causing the bridge regression: 7,305 dead .sock files, servers never unlinking on exit.\n\n- **Obsoleted by design** the same day: the human ruled the stdio MCP and the whole attach/unix-socket machinery out of existence (see stdio-retires) — no sockets minted means no litter.\n- The dispatched lane got as far as red tests + fixes with the unit suite green before the ruling; its work dies with the machinery.\n  - Salvage in the killed worktree's history if ever wanted.\n- **Cleanup:** the 7,305 existing files are a one-line janitor sweep for the human: rm /run/user/1000/olai/*.sock (live servers re-create theirs).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-process-leak","parent":"sbcbh1v3","ord":"a1","title":"A disconnected olai mcp never exits — four found alive from three builds","doing":true,"desc":"Found 2026-08-15: four `olai mcp docs` processes alive from three builds after their sessions disconnected.\n\n- **Obsoleted by design** the same day: the human ruled the stdio MCP subcommand out of existence (see stdio-retires) — no such process will exist to leak.\n- The four live orphans are the human's one-line janitor kill.\n- If the leak class resurfaces in some other subprocess, the stdin-end drain precedent is PR #94.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"ei35v8gv","parent":"9ljalyrf","ord":"a3","title":"Regressions"}
{"id":"bridge-no-fallback","parent":"ei35v8gv","ord":"a0","title":"PR: an attached olai mcp survives its server — solo-boot fallback on peer death","todo":true,"desc":"OFFENDING PR: #175.\n\n- The attached olai mcp inherited its server's lifetime with no fallback — three live ledger deaths in one hour proved it.\n- **Superseded by design** 2026-08-15, the same day it was filed: the human ruled the stdio MCP out of existence entirely (stdio-retires) — .mcp.json dials the running server over HTTP, so there is no attacher left to fall back.\n- **Worth keeping:** the design conversation that got here.\n  - Two stores over one directory have no cross-process protection: whole-file last-writer-wins, per-brain validation that breaks on disk, two git committers.\n  - So ONE BRAIN is the law — enforced henceforth by the directory lock (brain-lock) rather than by attach machinery.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-stdout-pollution","parent":"sbcbh1v3","ord":"a2","title":"olai mcp logs onto stdout — warnings corrupt the JSON-RPC pipe","desc":"Was: `olai mcp` logged warnings onto stdout, corrupting the JSON-RPC pipe. OBSOLETE 2026-08-15: PR #184 deleted the `olai mcp` subcommand entirely — there is no stdio pipe to corrupt. Agents dial the running server over HTTP, where logs and the protocol never share a stream."}
{"id":"now","parent":"9ljalyrf","ord":"a4","title":"Now","desc":"Ongoing work. Each entry is a MIRROR of the item being worked, so its mark, note and subtree reflect live — Workflowy-style. The tracking list (Kolu terminal, current #stage hashtag, PR link) lives on the item itself, where a mirror's four fields cannot."}
{"id":"htm-extension","parent":"wtanceuk","ord":"a1","title":"PR: .htm joins the registry — one line, the day somebody has one","todo":true,"desc":"Deferral from PR #189 (2026-08-15): kinds.ts:73 deliberately claims one spelling per kind, so .htm is unclaimed. The registry makes this exactly one entry (that being true was the point of the registry); a vault holding a real .htm is the trigger."}
{"id":"create-outline-root-nudge","parent":"sbcbh1v3","ord":"a3","title":"PR: create_outline refuses the served root's own name instead of minting docs/docs","todo":true,"desc":"Deferred twice from PR #182 with the shape argued (2026-08-15).\n\n- **Problem:** create_outline's path is judged through creatable (plan.ts:1477) against a Scope (plan.ts:216) that does not know where the served root is or what it is called.\n  - So `docs/agents.jsonl` handed to a server whose root IS docs minted docs/docs silently (it happened; a git mv undid it).\n- **Fix:** threads the served directory into Scope and through ops.ts — its own change, not a rider.\n- The refusal wants a sentence: a first path segment equaling the served root's own name is at least a nudge.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"stray-file-green-ci","parent":"sbcbh1v3","ord":"a4","title":"PR: CI fails on an unexplained new tracked file — green stops being blind to strays","todo":true,"desc":"Hazard proven live on PR #178 (2026-08-15).\n\n- **Evidence:** a reviewer's scratch file named `60` at the repo root was swept in by `git add -A` and NINE required CI lanes passed over it THREE times — green CI says nothing about files no test imports.\n- A person reading the tree caught it.\n- **Fix shape:** a required check (or claims-sweep arm) that fails when a PR adds a tracked file no manifest/test/doc accounts for.\n  - An allowlist of expected top-level entries at minimum, the tests/extension.test.ts sweep style.\n- **Counter-argument** to weigh in the PR: every legitimate new file pays a toll; the toll must be one obvious line, or the check will be resented and exempted to death.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"website-quiet-face","parent":"wtanceuk","ord":"a2","title":"The website's illustration still draws the pre-quiet outline — redraw it to match #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"#210's one deferral.\n\n- website/index.html's hand-written illustration still shows accent tag pills, an always-shown note line, and two gutter columns — the face #210 retired.\n- **Fix:** redraw it to the quiet face (dim inline tags, pilcrow, folded notes) once the design has settled in daily use.\n- It is an illustration, not the app, so it deliberately followed the design pass rather than preceding it.","created":"2026-08-16T17:19:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"7axjtuln","parent":"9ljalyrf","ord":"a5","title":"Editor"}
{"id":"md-rich-editing","parent":"7axjtuln","ord":"a0","title":"Rich-text markdown editing: write the document as it renders #needs-brainstorm","desc":"Filed 2026-08-13 on the human's word, immediately after #148 shipped plain-textarea editing.\n\n- **Next step:** editing the rendered document rather than its source — WYSIWYG-ish markdown (the class of ProseMirror/Milkdown/Tiptap, or olai's own take), where **bold** is bold while you type.\n- Deliberately OUT of #148's scope by its brief.\n- **To brainstorm before dispatch:**\n  - Source-of-truth fidelity (round-tripping markdown without rewriting the user's spelling — the files-are-the-database constraint applies to formatting too).\n  - Whether the plain textarea remains as an escape hatch.\n  - How the conflict/refusal story (#148's was-guard, Overwrite verb) carries over.\n  - Dependency weight vs olai's hand-rolled grammar.\n- **Brainstormed and answered 2026-08-18**, with the human — the dispatch-ready ruling is `md-live-preview-editor` (see).\n  - Fidelity is solved by construction: source stays the document model, Obsidian-style live preview; the ProseMirror/Milkdown/Tiptap class this node floated is ruled OUT for serializer round-trip churn.\n  - The was-guard and Overwrite carry over into autosave.\n  - The dependency question was ruled the other way round — dependencies are not cost, handrolled code is, so the behavior comes from ink-mde (fallback ixora) and our code is glue.\n- This node stays only as the paper trail of the question.","see":["md-live-preview-editor"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00"}
{"id":"colourful-palette","parent":"wtanceuk","ord":"a3","title":"A really colourful palette, nichely named","desc":"REJECTED by the human 2026-08-11 — work abandoned unmerged. Left unmarked on purpose: not done, and no longer anyone's task.\n\n- **The ask:** ONE new palette in theme/palettes.ts — saturated and vivid against the fifteen muted ones, 8+ visible hue families, niche one-word name, ink-on-paper AA per #69's precedent, picker-automatic.\n- **What happened:** two rounds never reached the ask — coruscant (near-monochrome purple), then prismatic (purple + orange two-tone). PR #107 closed, branch/worktree deleted, terminal killed. (Process had been: no review, orchestrator fields with screenshots at green CI.)\n- **What survives for a future attempt:** the 8-token system caps a pure palette at 8 hue families — each token must take its OWN family (the failed attempts tinted two); a docs page may need a palette-scoped mechanism beyond the tokens (syntax-highlight theme, heading ramp) to read as a spectrum.","see":["theming"]}
{"id":"whats-new","parent":"wtanceuk","ord":"a4","title":"What's new: the app tells you what changed, every PR, linking the PR","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 from the human's ask, ruled in discussion.\n\n- **Feature:** a \"What's new\" item in the APP HEADER with an unread dot (last-seen entry held via createPreference — the receptacle is there for exactly this).\n- Clicking opens the list of entries, newest first, each linking its PR (github.com/juspay/olai/pull/N).\n- **Ruled:** entries are HAND-WRITTEN, ONE PER PR — a data file every PR must touch, ENFORCED BY A CI CHECK.\n  - A PR that touches no entry fails, with an explicit skip marker for the rare PR that truly has nothing user-facing.\n- The generated-from-merge-subjects option was considered and declined: the human wants editorial control (prose beyond the title, screenshots possible), accepting the per-PR tax.\n- Entries render through the existing markdown pipeline — olai-native, no second renderer.\n- **Brief-time details:**\n  - The entry file's format and home.\n  - The CI check joins the odu pipeline.\n  - Orchestrator briefs must tell every author \"write your What's new entry\" once this ships.","created":"2026-08-19T13:36:53-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:28-04:00","custom":{"from":"human 2026-08-19"}}
{"id":"menu-under-headers","parent":"sbcbh1v3","ord":"a5","title":"The node context menu renders under section headers — the ••• menu is cut in two","doing":true,"desc":"Reported by the human with a screenshot, 2026-08-17 night.\n\n- **Bug:** open a node's ••• context menu (Zoom in / Ask agent / Copy link / marks / Set date / Add property / Link to a node / … / Copy as text) and scroll-adjacent content paints OVER it.\n- **In the capture:** the \"Viewing 46/48\" section header row cuts the menu in two (menu visible above and below the header; \"Move to Trash\" half-swallowed).\n- **Likely cause:** a stacking bug — the sticky section header creates a stacking context above the menu popover.\n- **Fix:** the menu must overlay everything while open.\n- **Screenshot** (if readable): /run/user/1000/kolu-523140/scratch/d4b8e3f6-0562-4129-adcd-7cae70e60f86/image.png","created":"2026-08-17T21:37:35-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:37:15-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/233"}}
