{"id":"perf-sweep-2026-08-24","parent":"umofmorh","ord":"a1","title":"The second O(n) sweep: what one keystroke still costs (2026-08-24)","desc":"A fresh whole-codebase audit (four parallel Opus reviewers, 2026-08-24), looking for work that grows with the whole vault (or the whole conversation) but is paid on every small event — a keystroke, a write, a stream frame, a tool call. The 2026-08-19 sweep's items were excluded and separately re-verified: three still true, one reworded (list_documents).\n\nThe one-line summary: **the browser is now clean — the server took over the walking.** The vault-in-browser series really did kill the client-side vault walks; what's left in the browser is page-sized. The heavy costs now live in the server's per-tab recomputation, in git-per-write, in the model's date/tag bookkeeping, and in a new family of chat-stream quadratics.\n\nEach child group is one area; each leaf is one standing cost with the evidence and a fix shape. Worst first within each group. Rough overall ranking: streams-per-tab and git-per-write dominate everything; the chat tool quadratic is what a long agent session feels; the agenda/tag costs grow with the vault's age.","see":["perf-sweep-2026-08-19","search-index"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","custom":{"from":"sweep by four parallel Opus subagents over format, server+surface, ops+chat, web client; findings verified per-event with file:line evidence"}}
{"id":"ihe1xcjp","parent":"umofmorh","ord":"a2","title":"Format & data model"}
{"id":"cskbbfmj","parent":"ihe1xcjp","ord":"a0","title":"The O(n) sweep: whole-corpus costs still paid per edit"}
{"id":"psw2-chat","parent":"cskbbfmj","ord":"a0","title":"Chat: streams that slow down as the conversation grows","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:30:03-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-tool-stream-quadratic","parent":"psw2-chat","ord":"a0","title":"A tool call's row re-sends everything-so-far on every stream frame — the quadratic the prose path already fixed","todo":true,"desc":"Prose got an appends path precisely to avoid re-sending the sum of its prefixes; tool rows didn't. Each tool_call_update re-publishes the whole row — cumulative output and the full pretty-printed JSON of input+output — so a call producing X bytes over N frames puts ~X·N on the wire (transcript.ts:842-1051), and the JSON is re-stringified per frame before a deep-compare decides nothing changed (agent.ts:2100, 613).\n\nFix shape: an appends path for tool progress, and serialize the detail once when the call settles.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-transcript-walks","parent":"psw2-chat","ord":"a1","title":"The panel re-walks the whole conversation on every tool frame and every turn","todo":true,"desc":"The open-question and armed-watcher counts iterate every row of the transcript ~3× per tool call (chat.ts:689-759), and the turn boundary walks all rows twice per turn (transcript.ts:637). Over a long agent session this is quadratic — the walks get longer as the conversation grows.\n\nFix shape: maintained counters and a remembered position, updated as rows change, instead of re-walking.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-chat-code-rescan","parent":"psw2-chat","ord":"a2","title":"The browser re-scans every code span of a streaming message, every frame","todo":true,"desc":"The node-reference marker runs querySelectorAll(\"code\") over the whole growing message on each throttled frame and re-tests every span (chat/refs.ts:190, Entry.tsx:196) — quadratic in one message's length. The comment admits the pass and optimises only the writes.\n\nFix shape: scan only what the frame appended.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"psw2-web","parent":"cskbbfmj","ord":"a1","title":"Browser: page-sized leftovers (the vault walks really are gone)","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:30:10-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-hide-done-copy","parent":"psw2-web","ord":"a0","title":"The \"hide done\" preference makes every write re-render the whole page","todo":true,"desc":"With the preference on, every arriving revision deep-copies every visible row (settings/done.ts:41 → derive.ts withoutDone's flatMap-spread). Spreading store proxies subscribes the memo to every field of every row and mints new objects for all of them — which defeats the keyed-merge fix, so one changed title re-runs ~25 bindings on every row. This is reactivity-after-the-flip's finding 2.11 come back through a different door.\n\nFix shape: hide without copying — filter by key, leave the row objects alone.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-filter-title-cache","parent":"psw2-web","ord":"a1","title":"Filtering re-parses every matched title on every keystroke — the cache defeats itself","todo":true,"desc":"The rendered-title cache puts the search terms INSIDE its cache key, so each keystroke turns every matched markdown title into a cache miss and a full markdown parse (markdown/title.ts:134-143) — the exact cost the cache's own header says it exists to refuse. The misses also flood the shared 1024-entry cache, whose overflow clears EVERYTHING, evicting the whole app's titles. Same trigger re-computes every matched note's excerpt per keystroke (NodeBody.tsx:133).\n\nFix shape: cache the parse by title alone; apply match-highlighting as a cheap step outside the cached parse.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-page-rescans","parent":"psw2-web","ord":"a2","title":"Smaller page-sized leftovers: drag, selection, caret, @-menu","todo":true,"desc":"Four milder ones, all bounded by the page or the file list rather than the vault: drag planning filters every placed row per pointer-move and runs 60×/s while the pointer parks at the autoscroll edge (drag/plan.ts:114, autoscroll.ts:157 — rows are y-sorted, a binary search is available); a held selection re-flattens the page on every revision for the whole duration of a bulk edit (select/selection.ts:150, admitted); an open caret costs one full flatten per arriving revision (edit/editing.tsx:287); and the chat @-menu scans every served path per keystroke (file/matching.ts:119).","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"ipwm8kle","parent":"cskbbfmj","ord":"a2","title":"Server: every open tab pays for every keystroke"}
{"id":"perf-narrowing-double-build","parent":"ipwm8kle","ord":"a0","title":"A tab with a filter open builds its page twice per write","todo":true,"desc":"The narrowing stream re-runs the exact same page construction the page stream just finished, and re-parses the filter text from scratch each time (runtime.ts:1007 → ops query.ts:416 → narrowingOf calling shownOf again). The comment claims \"the walk is the page's\" — it is a second page's.\n\nFix shape: derive the narrowing from the page answer that already exists; parse the filter once per text change, not once per revision.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-connect-firstframe","parent":"ipwm8kle","ord":"a1","title":"Opening or re-opening a tab ships the whole heads map and a full transcript copy","todo":true,"desc":"Each connect/reconnect encodes one entry per served file (runtime.ts:890) and copies the entire chat transcript and live pieces (runtime.ts:898, 928). Fine for one tab; a server restart with many tabs open is a reconnect storm paying O(tabs × files). Mild — listed so it is written down.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"cnbp0ix7","parent":"cskbbfmj","ord":"a3","title":"The model: costs that grow with the vault's age"}
{"id":"perf-move-picker-dfs","parent":"cnbp0ix7","ord":"a0","title":"The move picker re-walks the moved branch once per candidate, per keystroke","todo":true,"desc":"For each destination in the picker's result batch, movingOf re-runs an identical depth-first walk of everything the moved row draws, just to ask \"would this create a loop?\" (moving.ts:194, 247). The walks differ only in the destination being looked for.\n\nFix shape: walk once from the moved row, collect the reachable set, answer the whole batch against it.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00"}
{"id":"h6d3fkzo","ord":"aA","title":"orchestrator/agents.olai"}
{"id":"29i2zotw","parent":"h6d3fkzo","ord":"a0","title":"Agents"}
{"id":"experiment-kimi-k3","parent":"29i2zotw","ord":"a0","title":"Experiment (the human's, 2026-08-23): opencode + kimi-k3 as an implementing agent vs Claude Opus — observe only, compare at the end","doing":true,"desc":"**kolu-pr** — \"Mount `kolu surface` — the agent API as shell verbs\" (branch kolu-surface-face) — open by 10:52, i.e. ≤1h30m after first seen (09:22); the Opus baseline's first PR took 1h47m from dispatch","created":"2026-08-23T09:27:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T13:13:10-04:00","custom":{"baseline":"Claude Opus[1m] on lane-scli PR 1 (kolu#2205 @kolu/surface-cli): dispatched 16:09, PR open by 17:56 (1h47m), merged 22:10 (6h01m wall incl. kolu's /be gauntlet + two CI platforms + a redeploy stall ~8 min + an orchestrator venue ruling); 31 commits; 0 human interventions, 3 orchestrator rulings (venue ×2, /be process); 1 e2e flake rerun; 0 stop-and-asks. PR 2 (olai) in flight — its numbers will be added.","criteria":"wall-clock to first PR / to green / to merge; commits; human prompts answered (awaiting events); orchestrator/human rulings needed; review findings (must/should/nits) and how many rounds; CI reruns; context used at the end; scope honesty (deferrals, claims vs verified); tool friction (e.g. `pnpm: command not found` outside nix develop at 09:24)","observations":"09:22 first seen awaiting a 4-option prompt (the human answered); 09:24 working (pnpm outside the dev shell → not found → nix develop); context 111K. 09:57 still reading types, branch kolu-surface-face, context 195.9K (77%). 10:27 committing, context 90.7K (compacted/new session). 10:52 kolu#2206 \"Mount `kolu surface` — the agent API as shell verbs\" OPEN (≤1h30m from first sighting; Opus's first PR: 1h47m). 13:12 REPORTED DONE to the human: 5 commits, +1478/−161, draft; lanes it ran: kolu-mcp 85/85, kolu-cli 134/134, surface-cli 52/52, ci::unit 121, ci::daemon 363, just check + fmt, atlas rebuilt; GitHub Actions all green; evidence screenshot of the branch binary driving the production padi. Two honesty notes it volunteered: evidence captured locally not on a pu box; the full ci::default (Playwright e2e) NOT run — \"the odu MCP wasn't wired here\", only scoped lanes. No odu ci:: statuses posted at all (only GitHub's own checks) — so the PR has NOT been through kolu's /ci; its e2e is untested. Wall-clock 09:22→13:12 = 3h50m to a self-declared done without CI; context 187.7K at the end. Human prompts answered: ≥1 (09:22), plus whatever the human typed directly.","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2206","task":"as seen 09:24: prototyping `kolu surface <verb>` in packages/kolu-cli on top of @kolu/surface-cli (proto-surface.ts; Command.make('surface') with the padi's verbs) — the kolu-cli migration #2205 explicitly left out","terminal":"bd0a0a9d-c9a8-4ed5-87b8-b29df90e0650 (opencode, model kimi-k3 'Build' agent), kolu worktree kolu-surface-cli — the HUMAN drives it; the orchestrator NEVER sends input, only reads"}}
{"id":"lane-mde","parent":"ssbk0aum","ord":"a2","title":"md-live-preview-editor — markdown stops being a dumb text box (human reviews the PR)","todo":true,"desc":"The human's word 2026-08-18 (~11:2x): dispatch when one of the three running Opus authors (#239 agenda-spine, filter-row-says-why, kolu #2181) frees a slot.\n- **Roadmap node md-live-preview-editor carries the full ruled spec:**\n  - Source-as-model faithfulness (serializer editors ruled out by name).\n  - ink-mde first / ixora fallback.\n  - Glue-only handrolled surface (tag-pill widget delegating to titleParts, autosave wiring, theming, prefs toggle).\n  - Autosave superseding DocEditor.tsx's header ruling (rewrite the header).\n  - Note editor first, then document editor.\n  - Vim via @replit/codemirror-vim behind an olai.editor.vim pref, with the Esc conflict settled in keys.ts.\n- **MERGE POLICY OVERRIDE** (the human, 2026-08-18 ~11:3x): the human reviews this PR THEMSELVES.\n  - The agent-review pipeline still runs (grok + opencode post comments, findings addressed, CI green, evidence posted).\n  - The PR is FIELDED to the human and merges only on their word. Never auto-merge this lane.","created":"2026-08-18T11:19:33-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:05:21-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","parked":"2026-08-18, the human's ruling — draft PR #241, revisit in distant future; branch + reviews preserved","repo":"repo-olai","terminal":"47c1ea35-8649-4ca0-a51b-5e40a295dcce"}}
{"id":"qwe339fl","parent":"dr9hjzzh","ord":"a1","title":"Documents & markdown"}
{"id":"md-live-preview-editor","parent":"qwe339fl","ord":"a0","title":"Markdown editing gets live preview (parked — draft PR #241)","doing":true,"desc":"- Parked 2026-08-18 by the human (\"revisit in distant future\"); draft PR #241 holds the work, branch and both reviews preserved.\n- Goal: the note and document editors become rich markdown editors, Obsidian-style — syntax marks hide except around the caret.\n- Key ruling: the markdown SOURCE stays the document model; editors with their own model that serialize back (ProseMirror, TipTap, Lexical, Milkdown) are ruled out — round-trips rewrite bytes the user never touched and break verbatim storage.\n- Stack: ink-mde (CodeMirror 6, Solid component) first choice; fallback @codemirror/lang-markdown + ixora. Hand-written code is glue only: the #tag pill widget, autosave, theming, prefs toggle.\n- Autosave replaces Save/Cancel: debounced ~500ms plus flush on blur; every write conditional (`was`) so a concurrent agent edit refuses loudly instead of clobbering.\n- Ship the note editor first, then the document editor. Vim mode via @replit/codemirror-vim, off by default, in prefs.","created":"2026-08-18T11:16:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:02:45-04:00","custom":{"parked":"2026-08-18 by the human's ruling (\"unhappy with markdown editor, revisit in distant future\") — draft PR #241 holds the work, branch + both reviews preserved, ten evidence images on the attachments CDN"}}
